     "Blocks N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) glutamate receptors, typically by binding within the ion channel pore as a non-competitive antagonist. NMDA receptor blockade reduces excitatory glutamatergic neurotransmission, producing dissociative anesthesia, analgesia, and altered states of consciousness characterized by feelings of detachment from body and environment.": "Bloquea los receptores de glutamato N-metil-D-aspartato (NMDA), normalmente uniéndose dentro del poro del canal iónico como antagonista no competitivo. El bloqueo del receptor NMDA reduce la neurotransmisión glutamatérgica excitatoria, produciendo anestesia disociativa, analgesia y estados alterados de consciencia caracterizados por sensaciones de desconexión del cuerpo y del entorno.",
